WEBVTT

00:11.375 --> 00:13.875
[eerie music playing]

00:43.500 --> 00:49.708
[distorted dialogue]

00:55.667 --> 00:57.167
[footsteps running]

01:04.958 --> 01:06.542
[tense music playing]

01:07.625 --> 01:09.833
[panting]

01:24.417 --> 01:26.000
-Can I see?
-[Kirsh] Five previously

01:26.083 --> 01:29.208
undiscovered species collected,
but the crew lost containment.

01:29.292 --> 01:31.375
Look with your eyes.

02:08.167 --> 02:09.500
[screaming]

02:13.708 --> 02:15.583
-[shouting]
-[Curly] Hey! Throw it down!

02:23.792 --> 02:24.792
You okay?

02:27.833 --> 02:31.458
Why couldn't we keep our names?
When they made us.

02:33.208 --> 02:34.875
I don't know,
I think it's 'cause we're a secret.

02:35.625 --> 02:36.958
You know, like, they're all code names.

02:38.708 --> 02:42.375
How come Peter Pan?
Why didn't we get to choose?

02:44.333 --> 02:45.417
I don't know, sweetie. I…

02:46.333 --> 02:48.292
I think just 'cause Lost Boys,
you know, they don't grow up.

02:48.917 --> 02:51.292
But they put us in grown-up bodies.

02:51.875 --> 02:53.917
We're not even all boys, we're half girls.

02:56.333 --> 02:57.875
How come Wendy gets to be Wendy?

03:05.250 --> 03:06.542
Because Wendy was the first.

03:07.625 --> 03:08.750
Nibs is a good name.

03:10.000 --> 03:12.167
You know, in the book,
they called Curly "Pickles."

03:12.250 --> 03:14.417
She's always getting into trouble,
you know? Like, "into a pickle."

03:15.375 --> 03:16.875
Well, at least Curly was in on the action.

03:19.792 --> 03:23.708
Tootles always missed everything
'cause he stepped off round the corner.

03:24.292 --> 03:25.542
[Kirsh] Quiet now.

03:25.625 --> 03:27.083
[ringing through intercom]

03:29.125 --> 03:30.333
Kirsh.

03:30.417 --> 03:32.375
[Boy Cavalier] Assume
I know everything from the feed.

03:32.458 --> 03:34.417
This is no longer a rescue mission.

03:34.500 --> 03:36.625
I want you to secure the site,

03:36.708 --> 03:39.417
collect alien life forms,
and bring them back for study.

03:39.500 --> 03:41.250
Boss, as much as I'd love to--

03:41.333 --> 03:42.417
S-Sir, I think--

03:42.500 --> 03:44.167
[Boy Cavalier]
Enough with the "I know better."

03:44.750 --> 03:46.292
[stammers, chuckles]

03:46.375 --> 03:50.500
A trillion dollars of R and D
just landed in our laps.

03:51.625 --> 03:53.917
She fucked up, Yutani,
so we're supposed to what?

03:54.000 --> 03:56.500
Just say, "All good,"
and give her her bioweapons back?

03:56.583 --> 04:00.792
Sir, we are weeks away from launching
a product that will change the world.

04:00.875 --> 04:03.625
-Boss, these are very dangerous--
-Oh, please, please,

04:03.708 --> 04:06.292
we have a high quarantine lab
in the sublevels.

04:06.375 --> 04:07.625
You said it yourself.

04:07.708 --> 04:11.167
It's five species. We bag them, isolate,

04:11.250 --> 04:12.875
do a full workup.

04:12.958 --> 04:13.958
How are my kids?

04:14.042 --> 04:16.875
I have three of them with me.
They've done well so far.

04:16.958 --> 04:18.667
-[Boy Cavalier] Including Wendy?
-[groans]

04:19.417 --> 04:22.000
-Kirsh?
-No, she went to find her brother.

04:23.083 --> 04:25.125
Oh, so she's just out there on her own.

04:25.208 --> 04:26.417
I sent Slightly with her.

04:27.708 --> 04:30.292
He's a child. I told you to watch her.
Her, specifically.

04:30.375 --> 04:33.333
Sir, with all due respect,
it's a crash site,

04:33.417 --> 04:35.500
and we're trying to contain
an alien invasion.

04:36.167 --> 04:38.083
I thought you were supposed
to be better than a man,

04:38.167 --> 04:40.542
but all I'm hearing are excuses.

04:40.625 --> 04:42.958
Bring her in. Now.

04:44.000 --> 04:45.000
[line clicks]

04:46.042 --> 04:50.292
So Wendy's just out there?
With all these things?

04:57.333 --> 04:58.833
[dramatic music playing]

05:11.208 --> 05:13.208
[sirens wailing]

05:14.375 --> 05:16.000
Joe! [panting]

05:16.708 --> 05:18.792
-J--
-[alien clicking]

05:20.750 --> 05:22.958
Joe. [panting]

05:23.875 --> 05:25.917
-[crashes]
-[alien clicking]

05:30.375 --> 05:31.375
Joe!

05:33.417 --> 05:35.667
[Hermit] No, Marcy!

05:36.333 --> 05:37.958
-It's a trap!
-Joe!

05:40.250 --> 05:42.125
-[Hermit] No!
-Joe!

05:45.667 --> 05:46.750
Joe.

05:49.542 --> 05:50.875
[Hermit] No. No, no, no.

05:52.167 --> 05:53.167
Marcy.

05:53.250 --> 05:54.667
[groans, panting]

05:55.458 --> 05:57.208
-[groans] Jesus.
-I got you.

05:57.292 --> 05:59.042
-I got you.
-Marcy, you've got to get out of here.

05:59.125 --> 06:01.208
-[grunts]
-It's coming back.

06:01.292 --> 06:02.292
[Marcy grunting]

06:03.167 --> 06:05.083
-Marcy.
-[grunts, panting]

06:05.833 --> 06:07.583
-Marcy. Marcy!
-[grunts]

06:11.417 --> 06:12.792
[alien hissing]

06:12.875 --> 06:14.667
[breathing heavily]

06:19.708 --> 06:22.542
[growling]

06:28.000 --> 06:29.500
Well, stay behind me.

06:29.583 --> 06:32.042
-I'm the soldier. You're a kid.
-Not anymore.

06:32.125 --> 06:33.125
Marcy.

06:33.208 --> 06:34.458
[alien clicking]

06:35.542 --> 06:37.000
[hissing]

06:47.375 --> 06:48.375
-Should we--
-No.

06:52.708 --> 06:55.417
[banging on ceiling]

07:00.875 --> 07:02.083
[banging stops]

07:10.958 --> 07:13.250
-[grunts]
-[alien screeching]

07:15.792 --> 07:17.292
Why is it doing that?

07:19.458 --> 07:20.792
It's acid.

07:24.833 --> 07:26.958
-We gotta get out of here.
-[banging on ceiling]

07:27.042 --> 07:29.750
[both grunting, panting]

07:35.083 --> 07:36.375
[alien screeches]

07:39.333 --> 07:40.375
[grunts]

07:42.250 --> 07:43.250
Marcy.

07:43.917 --> 07:45.458
[screeching]

07:53.375 --> 07:54.375
[whispers] Marcy.

08:10.250 --> 08:11.333
Marcy.

08:30.583 --> 08:33.417
-[grunts, screams]
-[alien growls]

08:38.500 --> 08:40.750
[grunts, coughs]

08:45.250 --> 08:47.167
[gasps, shudders]

08:47.250 --> 08:48.500
[growls]

08:55.375 --> 08:56.625
[alien screeching]

09:00.083 --> 09:02.542
-What are you doing?
-I don't know!

09:04.458 --> 09:05.542
Joe, the door!

09:07.375 --> 09:09.208
Get to the door!

09:09.292 --> 09:10.708
[grunts]

09:14.500 --> 09:15.667
[Marcy] Joe!

09:20.375 --> 09:21.625
[grunts]

09:25.042 --> 09:26.208
Ready? [grunts]

09:30.292 --> 09:32.250
-Now!
-[door buzzes]

09:38.250 --> 09:39.500
Marcy!

09:39.583 --> 09:40.917
[buzzer sounds]

09:41.000 --> 09:43.708
Marcy! Marcy!

09:43.792 --> 09:45.208
-[Marcy grunting]
-[alien screeching]

09:47.292 --> 09:49.167
[Marcy grunting, screaming]

09:49.250 --> 09:51.125
-[thuds]
-I'm coming!

09:51.208 --> 09:52.292
[Marcy grunts]

09:53.542 --> 09:55.167
[door buzzing]

09:55.250 --> 09:57.375
-[bell ringing]
-Come on, come on, come on.

10:03.417 --> 10:05.167
-[door buzzing]
-Fuck. Marcy!

10:07.917 --> 10:08.917
[grunting]

10:10.250 --> 10:11.375
Marcy.

10:37.875 --> 10:38.875
No.

10:41.417 --> 10:42.875
No, no, no.

10:45.292 --> 10:46.875
[gags, coughs blood]

10:48.292 --> 10:51.250
[breathing heavily]
Marcy. Marcy. You're gonna be okay.

10:52.083 --> 10:53.500
[stammering]

10:56.292 --> 10:59.792
You're gonna be okay.
Marcy, I'm here, okay?

10:59.875 --> 11:01.125
[breathing heavily]

11:01.875 --> 11:03.667
[groans, choking]

11:05.375 --> 11:07.833
Stay with me. Stay… [breathing heavily]

11:37.208 --> 11:38.333
Wendy?

11:38.417 --> 11:41.583
[ominous music playing]

11:48.875 --> 11:50.292
[squelches]

12:04.583 --> 12:06.208
[glass shatters]

12:17.167 --> 12:18.333
[metal thuds]

12:26.250 --> 12:28.167
[sighs] Bro! [groans]

12:28.667 --> 12:29.708
Finally.

12:30.417 --> 12:31.917
Kirsh wants you, bro.

12:32.000 --> 12:33.917
You scared the shit out of me, bro!

12:34.000 --> 12:36.333
-[Smee] Hey! Hey! What are you doing?
-What's wrong with you?

12:38.458 --> 12:40.083
[Smee] Ah! All right.

12:40.167 --> 12:41.167
[both grunting]

12:41.250 --> 12:42.500
[Smee] Sorry, bro.

12:43.917 --> 12:45.458
It's creepy as fuck out there, bro.

12:45.542 --> 12:47.375
[both breathing heavily]

12:47.458 --> 12:49.375
-You said fuck.
-You said shit.

12:52.792 --> 12:54.792
[both chuckling]

12:57.792 --> 12:58.792
-Bro.
-Yeah?

12:58.875 --> 13:01.708
-Can you believe we're on a spaceship?
-Yeah, underground,

13:01.792 --> 13:04.167
which is a dumb ass place
to put a spaceship if you ask me.

13:04.250 --> 13:05.375
Pfft.

13:05.458 --> 13:06.458
Wait. [stammers]

13:08.083 --> 13:09.083
What are those?

13:10.042 --> 13:11.042
Eggs, I think.

13:12.875 --> 13:14.875
-Ah! Dude. Oh!
-What?

13:14.958 --> 13:15.958
-What?
-Dude.

13:16.042 --> 13:18.792
We saw this, like… this, like, space bugs…

13:18.875 --> 13:21.125
-Space bugs?
-…that drink, like, all your blood.

13:21.208 --> 13:22.208
-What?
-Right?

13:22.292 --> 13:24.833
And then we saw
this super messed up, like,

13:25.625 --> 13:27.917
-octopus eye monster.
-Octopus?

13:28.000 --> 13:29.000
Dude, come on.

13:29.083 --> 13:30.833
-I can't believe I missed that.
-Bro. Bro.

13:32.333 --> 13:33.458
It tried to yoke Nibs.

13:33.542 --> 13:34.625
-No. Come…
-It was like…

13:34.708 --> 13:36.750
[grunts, yells]

13:36.833 --> 13:38.708
-Like, bro.
-Aw, dude…

13:38.792 --> 13:40.667
-It was full-on sci-fi.
-That sucks.

13:40.750 --> 13:42.417
-Bro. Wait.
-[groans]

13:42.500 --> 13:44.208
-I should've been there.
-Where's Wendy?

13:44.750 --> 13:45.958
-Dude!
-What?

13:46.042 --> 13:49.208
This 12-foot-tall alien thing,
it just took her brother from there.

13:49.792 --> 13:52.750
And she's gone all
hunter-killer mode now in pursuit.

13:52.833 --> 13:53.875
Wait, alone?

13:53.958 --> 13:55.833
She said stay here. I would have gone.

13:56.417 --> 13:57.917
-Huh.
-Yeah.

13:58.000 --> 14:00.583
What do you think
is in these eggs, like, really?

14:01.167 --> 14:02.375
-Not chickens.
-[chuckles]

14:02.458 --> 14:04.208
-Check this out.
-What? Check this out.

14:04.292 --> 14:05.792
-[person] Turn around.
-I can--

14:05.875 --> 14:07.375
Slowly.

14:11.667 --> 14:12.750
Drop your guns.

14:13.875 --> 14:15.333
[Smee] We don't have any guns.

14:15.417 --> 14:17.375
-[Slightly] Yeah, they don't let us.
-[whispers] Shut up.

14:17.458 --> 14:18.833
-[Slightly] It's okay.
-No, it's not.

14:19.542 --> 14:20.958
Move away from the eggs.

14:22.792 --> 14:25.542
Slowly. Over to me.

14:29.417 --> 14:30.458
Mm-mmm.

14:34.000 --> 14:35.458
Where are we?

14:35.542 --> 14:37.458
What do you mean? A spaceship.

14:38.125 --> 14:40.000
No, where? What city?

14:40.083 --> 14:42.708
It's a Prodigy city. It starts…
It starts with a S.

14:42.792 --> 14:43.875
[both] Um…

14:45.042 --> 14:46.917
-Uh… New Siam.
-New Siam.

14:47.000 --> 14:48.667
-Yeah. Yeah.
-New Siam. I knew it.

14:49.583 --> 14:51.833
What, is this… is this your ship?
Did you crash?

14:51.917 --> 14:53.625
-That must have hurt.
-[Slightly] Did it hurt?

14:53.708 --> 14:54.792
Quiet.

14:55.375 --> 14:56.458
[whispers indistinctly]

14:57.417 --> 14:59.417
-You're like a couple of kids.
-[Slightly groans]

14:59.500 --> 15:01.917
-We are not kids!
-Yeah, no, we're not.

15:02.542 --> 15:04.083
[both] We're not kids.

15:12.083 --> 15:13.292
What are you doing here?

15:14.083 --> 15:15.500
Do you come for the specimen?

15:16.333 --> 15:17.417
Um…

15:17.500 --> 15:19.250
-That's… classified.
-It's classified.

15:19.333 --> 15:20.958
Yeah, it's classified.

15:23.250 --> 15:25.792
All right. Um…

15:27.542 --> 15:28.917
[clicks tongue] Here's a scenario.

15:29.875 --> 15:32.458
You're the chief security officer
on a… on a ship.

15:32.958 --> 15:34.958
A deep space research vessel.

15:35.750 --> 15:39.250
So, this ship finds something

15:39.875 --> 15:41.458
on a faraway moon.

15:43.083 --> 15:44.125
Eggs.

15:45.250 --> 15:48.167
Wait, like, these eggs?

15:48.250 --> 15:53.208
Right. These eggs,
they're not like normal eggs.

15:54.167 --> 15:56.625
And when you take them onto the ship,
they start to hatch.

15:57.375 --> 15:59.042
And monsters come out.

16:01.375 --> 16:02.750
You've met them, I think.

16:03.708 --> 16:04.833
The monsters.

16:06.708 --> 16:07.708
Um…

16:07.792 --> 16:11.542
-I think we should…
-I think… Yeah, um… Sorry, we're…

16:13.458 --> 16:14.708
Okay. Sorry… We're just…

16:25.833 --> 16:27.333
-[whispers] Let's go.
-[whispers] Let's go.

16:27.417 --> 16:31.750
There's a feeling you get in this scenario

16:32.625 --> 16:35.542
when the monsters come and you can't…

16:36.042 --> 16:37.625
[computer beeps]

16:38.542 --> 16:40.458
…you don't help.

16:40.542 --> 16:42.542
[machinery whirring]

16:45.000 --> 16:47.250
[Mother] Commencing data transfer.

16:51.875 --> 16:53.250
Maybe you're feeling it now.

16:54.333 --> 16:58.333
When Mother says
the crew's life don't matter,

16:58.417 --> 17:00.583
only the bounty matters.

17:01.625 --> 17:07.292
When you hear the screams,
and all you can do is save yourself.

17:11.042 --> 17:12.167
Are you a robot?

17:12.250 --> 17:13.708
[chuckles]

17:13.792 --> 17:14.917
Wouldn't that be nice?

17:15.542 --> 17:17.458
To be all machine instead of what I am.

17:18.167 --> 17:19.500
The worst parts of a man.

17:20.292 --> 17:23.542
[Mother] Data transfer at 78%.

17:23.625 --> 17:25.583
So… [breathing heavily]

17:25.667 --> 17:26.667
What…

17:27.792 --> 17:29.458
What would you do?

17:29.542 --> 17:30.792
In the scenario.

17:31.500 --> 17:35.542
Could you harm others
or allow them to be harmed?

17:36.250 --> 17:37.625
Could you follow those orders?

17:38.958 --> 17:41.375
-No, not, like…
-Are they bad people?

17:42.750 --> 17:43.833
Does it matter?

17:45.417 --> 17:47.125
Yeah. I mean, you know,

17:47.208 --> 17:50.542
if it was to protect someone
like… like a friend or--

17:50.625 --> 17:53.500
Like our… Like our parents.

17:53.583 --> 17:55.708
Yeah. Like our parents.

17:55.792 --> 17:59.917
[Mother] Data transfer at 93%.

18:00.000 --> 18:01.042
You don't know.

18:01.917 --> 18:03.167
Is that possible?

18:03.750 --> 18:04.833
Know what?

18:04.917 --> 18:09.625
Well, your bodies are clearly synthetic,
but you think you have parents.

18:10.208 --> 18:12.250
-Oh, no. It's just 'cause we…
-[whispers] No. Don't. Shh.

18:12.333 --> 18:13.458
Don't tell him.

18:14.542 --> 18:15.792
Tell me what?

18:16.667 --> 18:19.750
-Nothing.
-[Mother] Data transfer at 98%.

18:20.708 --> 18:22.000
Ninety-nine.

18:22.833 --> 18:24.333
100.

18:24.417 --> 18:25.417
[pants]

18:25.500 --> 18:28.583
-Data transfer complete.
-[machinery powering down]

18:28.667 --> 18:31.125
Data erased from source.

18:32.542 --> 18:33.542
[interface chimes]

18:38.000 --> 18:39.375
Tell me what?

18:41.917 --> 18:43.375
[grunting]

18:44.875 --> 18:46.542
When is a machine not a machine?

18:48.375 --> 18:49.625
[choking] Get off me.

18:49.708 --> 18:52.417
When is a machine not a machine?

18:53.250 --> 18:54.833
[Slightly choking]

18:54.917 --> 18:55.917
Let him go.

18:57.000 --> 18:58.458
[Slightly breathing heavily]

18:59.542 --> 19:01.167
Ah! He has a gun.

19:01.750 --> 19:03.208
I can see that.

19:03.292 --> 19:04.750
Hey. You're on my ship.

19:05.708 --> 19:10.750
This ship, to be clear,
is an object, not a location.

19:10.833 --> 19:14.083
It's a ball that got hit over the fence
into the neighbor's yard.

19:14.167 --> 19:17.833
I'm the neighbor,
so the ship belongs to me now.

19:18.667 --> 19:21.125
-You're Prodigy?
-I work for Prodigy.

19:22.125 --> 19:23.417
I don't talk to errand boys.

19:23.500 --> 19:26.125
And which country are you king of again?

19:27.333 --> 19:28.333
Are you the parent?

19:28.417 --> 19:29.542
Excuse me?

19:31.292 --> 19:33.125
These synths,
they think they have parents.

19:33.208 --> 19:34.208
Are you the parent?

19:34.292 --> 19:38.167
We're not here to talk about
what I am, Mr. Morrow.

19:42.000 --> 19:43.375
I read the manifest.

19:43.458 --> 19:46.042
Chief of security. Sole survivor. Cyborg.

19:46.625 --> 19:48.458
Lost a lot of friends, did you?

19:48.542 --> 19:49.833
I don't have friends.

19:49.917 --> 19:51.708
Everybody needs friends.

19:54.875 --> 19:56.333
She won't let you have them.

19:57.833 --> 20:03.833
What's on this ship, she spent billions.
People's lives. They belong to her.

20:03.917 --> 20:07.375
[eggs rumbling]

20:09.583 --> 20:12.833
If you're not careful,
you're gonna belong to them.

20:12.917 --> 20:15.792
[tense music plays]

20:16.958 --> 20:18.458
[alien screeches]

20:24.625 --> 20:26.542
-Dude. Dude.
-No!

20:39.917 --> 20:42.417
[gentle music playing]

20:48.542 --> 20:50.458
[truck beeping]

20:52.833 --> 20:55.417
[machinery humming]

21:00.125 --> 21:02.833
[yelling]

21:02.917 --> 21:04.833
[music continues]

21:15.125 --> 21:17.792
We've swept the crash site.
No sign of the cyborg.

21:45.333 --> 21:48.708
-[radio chatter]
-[clicking lips]

22:07.917 --> 22:10.500
[heart monitor beeping]

22:27.833 --> 22:30.833
[music continues]

23:42.125 --> 23:44.125
[gentle music fades]

23:44.208 --> 23:46.708
[sinister music plays]

24:30.875 --> 24:32.292
[machinery beeping]

24:34.458 --> 24:36.292
-[Dame Sylvia] Is she gonna--
-Just give me a second.

24:36.875 --> 24:38.208
I need a full firmware review.

24:38.292 --> 24:40.500
Loop in the skeletal team.
They'll scan for microfractures.

24:42.083 --> 24:43.417
This is my fault.

24:43.500 --> 24:45.083
It's no one's fault. She made a choice.

24:45.167 --> 24:46.833
She's a child.

24:46.917 --> 24:48.333
I'm her guardian.

24:49.125 --> 24:51.833
He made a choice, not you.

24:52.708 --> 24:53.958
And he's the boss, but…

24:54.833 --> 24:56.750
If you ask me,
sending a… a billion-dollar prototype

24:56.833 --> 24:59.000
-to an active crash site is--
-[Boy Kavalier] What?

25:01.250 --> 25:02.333
Nothing.

25:07.625 --> 25:09.125
-Yeah, nothing.
-[Boy Kavalier] No?

25:11.000 --> 25:12.083
What were you gonna say?

25:17.250 --> 25:20.125
Look, it's your company.
You can decide whatever you wanna do.

25:20.208 --> 25:21.583
Please, grow a spine.

25:21.667 --> 25:22.667
Enough.

25:26.375 --> 25:27.625
What happened happened.

25:29.375 --> 25:32.083
And she was so brave, our girl.

25:32.167 --> 25:34.542
I can't even believe it,
but she took a lot of damage.

25:34.625 --> 25:37.000
So if you could just please
let us get on with our jobs.

25:37.083 --> 25:39.583
-Can you save her?
-Yeah, I'm doing tests right now.

25:41.333 --> 25:42.625
-Can I talk to her?
-No.

25:43.667 --> 25:45.292
No. Kirsh suspended her hardware
at the site.

25:45.375 --> 25:46.542
It seemed the safest option.

25:46.625 --> 25:49.208
I'm looking at her here.
I'm worried about that, okay?

26:02.875 --> 26:03.875
Careful.

26:13.083 --> 26:14.250
Fascinating.

26:15.083 --> 26:16.167
You can go.

26:23.417 --> 26:24.542
Well done, you two.

26:34.583 --> 26:35.667
Was it worth it?

26:38.083 --> 26:39.083
What?

26:40.875 --> 26:43.917
Risking a decade's work
on something new and shiny.

26:44.542 --> 26:47.083
My, you're all so feisty today.

26:48.292 --> 26:49.375
[Boy Kavalier scoffs]

26:51.625 --> 26:53.083
I thought you'd be excited.

26:57.875 --> 26:59.500
All this ground to break.

27:02.250 --> 27:03.542
New life-forms.

27:04.583 --> 27:07.250
With acid for blood. [chuckles]

27:08.875 --> 27:11.417
Like an undiscovered country.

27:14.542 --> 27:15.750
And here you are.

27:17.458 --> 27:18.792
A scientist.

27:30.500 --> 27:32.667
-Out.
-Hey. Hey. Hey.

27:34.417 --> 27:35.458
Out.

27:36.667 --> 27:38.458
-Hey.
-[knocks on door]

27:38.542 --> 27:39.542
What the fuck?

27:39.625 --> 27:40.667
It's a parasite.

27:40.750 --> 27:42.625
The Xenomorph lays its eggs.

27:42.708 --> 27:46.583
They wait for organic life to draw near,
only to hatch some kind of proto-creature.

27:46.667 --> 27:47.667
How do you know that?

27:47.750 --> 27:50.667
I saw it earlier
with the security officer.

27:51.625 --> 27:54.750
The body in the cryotube
was killed from the inside.

27:54.833 --> 27:57.958
The proto-creatures must have gestated
inside a human host.

28:02.000 --> 28:03.042
Like you.

28:06.500 --> 28:07.542
Lock it down.

28:09.542 --> 28:11.417
Nobody in or out who isn't synthetic.

28:12.917 --> 28:14.208
You're in charge.

28:17.875 --> 28:18.875
As you wish.

28:40.208 --> 28:41.417
Psst.

29:00.000 --> 29:01.875
Um… [stammers]

29:01.958 --> 29:03.292
Are we in trouble?

29:04.458 --> 29:05.792
[smacks lips] Why?

29:07.167 --> 29:08.375
Have you done something?

29:08.958 --> 29:10.125
[stammers]

29:11.625 --> 29:12.750
No, sir.

29:12.833 --> 29:14.625
Exactly what we were told.

29:20.125 --> 29:24.250
Tell me about this security officer
that you encountered.

29:25.917 --> 29:27.000
Um…

29:28.208 --> 29:31.542
Well, he had a… he had a knife in his arm.

29:34.125 --> 29:36.167
Yeah, like a… like a robot arm,

29:36.250 --> 29:38.500
and he… he threatened Slightly.

29:39.375 --> 29:40.708
Well, both of us really.

29:40.792 --> 29:42.458
Yeah, but it was my neck.

29:42.542 --> 29:44.542
Yeah, but after he'd done you,
he would've done me as well.

29:44.625 --> 29:46.042
-Well, then he…
-Quiet.

29:50.583 --> 29:52.167
There's no sign of him at the site.

29:52.958 --> 29:54.875
We think he managed
to slip through the cordon.

29:56.125 --> 29:59.583
We're circulating images we took
from your retinal cameras.

30:00.583 --> 30:01.708
Our what?

30:02.625 --> 30:03.667
Your eyes.

30:05.000 --> 30:06.917
We record everything you see.

30:08.833 --> 30:11.125
[chuckles] Like, shut up. Really?

30:12.542 --> 30:14.000
I don't think I like that.

30:14.750 --> 30:16.708
There's one thing I didn't catch though.

30:18.542 --> 30:20.625
What did he whisper to you?

30:20.708 --> 30:21.750
At the end.

30:24.667 --> 30:25.667
Uh…

30:28.208 --> 30:31.333
He said,
"When is a machine not a machine?"

30:35.292 --> 30:36.625
[scoffs]

30:40.625 --> 30:42.375
[scoffs] Fine.

30:44.500 --> 30:45.958
[clicks tongue] That's all for now.

30:49.875 --> 30:51.833
Uh, y-you'll find him though, right?

30:54.375 --> 30:56.292
Like, h-he's not gonna…

30:56.792 --> 30:57.792
Um…

30:59.458 --> 31:00.500
Going to what?

31:01.375 --> 31:02.500
I-I don't know.

31:03.083 --> 31:05.375
Like, come here, kill us in our sleep.

31:09.042 --> 31:10.208
Of course not.

31:11.125 --> 31:14.042
This is a secure facility
in the middle of an ocean.

31:15.125 --> 31:16.125
No.

31:17.083 --> 31:18.125
Trust me.

31:19.250 --> 31:22.542
He'll be dead or in custody
by the day's end.

31:24.875 --> 31:27.208
-[door opens, closes]
-Thank you.

32:01.667 --> 32:04.417
[siren wailing in distance]

32:05.250 --> 32:07.250
[engine whirring]

32:07.333 --> 32:09.083
[people chattering]

32:27.625 --> 32:29.625
[baby crying]

32:33.458 --> 32:35.083
[phone beeping]

32:37.875 --> 32:40.000
-[ringing]
-[sighs]

32:40.083 --> 32:41.250
[person] Weyland-Yutani.

32:41.792 --> 32:46.417
Security code 871. Key word: Falcon.

32:46.917 --> 32:48.750
-[dog barking]
-Hold, please.

32:51.333 --> 32:52.708
Mr. Morrow.

32:52.792 --> 32:54.167
[Morrow] Who is this?

32:54.250 --> 32:56.208
Do you have my specimens?

32:57.250 --> 32:58.917
I need to speak with Yutani.

32:59.542 --> 33:01.125
I have code word clearance.

33:01.208 --> 33:02.292
[Yutani] This is her.

33:04.042 --> 33:07.083
Ah. I see. Yes.

33:07.958 --> 33:10.292
You used to know my grandmother.

33:11.333 --> 33:13.542
It's been 65 years, Mr. Morrow.

33:14.458 --> 33:16.125
I run the enterprise today.

33:17.583 --> 33:18.708
Now,

33:19.458 --> 33:21.000
where are my creatures?

33:22.083 --> 33:24.625
Captured, but I have the data.

33:25.292 --> 33:26.417
The data is good,

33:26.500 --> 33:27.500
but it's not enough.

33:27.583 --> 33:28.625
Did they survive?

33:29.208 --> 33:31.917
Yes. We were sabotaged.

33:32.000 --> 33:34.375
Come in and we'll do a full debrief.

33:37.625 --> 33:38.875
Who is Prodigy?

33:38.958 --> 33:42.167
A rival, run by a child.

33:42.708 --> 33:44.250
I can get them back.

33:44.333 --> 33:45.833
I see a way in.

33:45.917 --> 33:48.500
No. You've done enough. Come home.

33:49.667 --> 33:50.958
I don't have a home.

33:51.625 --> 33:53.917
I'm gone a lifetime.
Everyone I know is dead.

33:54.625 --> 33:58.083
Yes, well,
you should have read your contract.

33:58.167 --> 33:59.250
I'm not complaining.

34:00.042 --> 34:01.542
I'm just telling you.

34:01.625 --> 34:02.875
This…

34:02.958 --> 34:05.292
These creatures, they are my life's work.

34:06.000 --> 34:07.417
And I'm gonna get them back.

34:08.208 --> 34:09.292
[phone chimes]

34:17.875 --> 34:20.500
[announcer] Prodigy is forever.

34:21.000 --> 34:23.000
Prodigy is…

34:40.625 --> 34:42.250
They're running tests on her now.

34:43.458 --> 34:44.792
I assume that's why you're here.

34:46.167 --> 34:48.000
You sent us on a mission.
I'm here to report.

34:48.083 --> 34:49.917
I sent Wendy on a mission.

34:51.667 --> 34:53.083
But she got broken.

34:55.833 --> 34:57.000
So here you are.

35:01.792 --> 35:03.042
She's your favorite.

35:04.042 --> 35:05.167
Says who?

35:07.917 --> 35:10.333
Smart people don't ask dumb questions,
I thought.

35:16.250 --> 35:19.542
She's my favorite
because she was the first.

35:22.417 --> 35:25.000
My dad always threw the first pancake
in the trash.

35:27.042 --> 35:28.042
[scoffs]

35:32.667 --> 35:33.875
Is this where you made us?

35:36.708 --> 35:39.292
Yeah. Does that bother you?

35:39.375 --> 35:40.458
No.

35:43.000 --> 35:45.167
Not everyone would like that, you know.

35:46.417 --> 35:49.167
Being artificial suddenly. [chuckles]

35:50.625 --> 35:51.708
No more blood.

35:53.417 --> 35:54.625
No more heart.

35:55.875 --> 35:57.917
-No more pooping.
-[chuckles]

36:01.167 --> 36:03.167
I'm okay with that
if I get to live forever.

36:05.583 --> 36:06.750
But does it…

36:06.833 --> 36:08.125
Does it… does it bother you?

36:09.000 --> 36:10.792
That Wendy's my favorite?

36:10.875 --> 36:12.250
No.

36:12.333 --> 36:14.125
I just think you're wrong. I'm the best.

36:14.208 --> 36:16.083
[scoffs] Really? Why?

36:17.500 --> 36:19.708
All she cares about is her stupid brother.

36:20.250 --> 36:21.458
But I think about things.

36:22.917 --> 36:24.125
What kind of things?

36:24.208 --> 36:25.208
The world.

36:25.917 --> 36:27.667
How to make it better. I have ideas.

36:28.417 --> 36:29.542
What kind of ideas?

36:31.750 --> 36:34.083
No way. If I tell you, you'll steal them.

36:35.708 --> 36:36.833
True.

36:39.667 --> 36:41.583
I'm saying I think I could be you one day.

36:42.208 --> 36:43.583
More than you maybe.

36:44.500 --> 36:45.958
But she doesn't care about that.

36:47.333 --> 36:49.708
You know,
and you gave us these big brains or the…

36:49.792 --> 36:51.167
this hard drive or whatever.

36:51.792 --> 36:52.792
Memory.

36:56.083 --> 36:57.333
I learned French.

36:58.625 --> 37:00.167
-When?
-Last week.

37:00.750 --> 37:02.458
I asked Arthur to upload all the lessons.

37:02.542 --> 37:04.083
[speaking French]

37:07.750 --> 37:09.083
Do you know what a prodigy is?

37:11.000 --> 37:12.708
Sure. A child genius.

37:13.292 --> 37:14.292
Yeah.

37:15.083 --> 37:21.208
But what most people don't understand
is what makes them geniuses

37:21.292 --> 37:23.583
is the fact that they're children.

37:25.125 --> 37:28.917
Because children have access

37:29.000 --> 37:33.250
to a world of infinite imagination.

37:36.250 --> 37:37.375
Like me.

37:39.542 --> 37:40.542
Like you.

37:43.625 --> 37:45.542
[chuckles] Tell you what.

37:47.125 --> 37:50.583
I'm gonna give you some books to read,

37:52.083 --> 37:55.667
some recordings to listen to,
some things to think about.

37:57.125 --> 38:00.250
And then we can get together

38:01.375 --> 38:04.292
and play.

38:05.792 --> 38:06.917
How's that sound?

38:08.000 --> 38:09.500
Does this mean I'm your favorite now?

38:10.333 --> 38:11.333
No.

38:13.708 --> 38:15.250
But you're in the race.

38:33.958 --> 38:35.375
[water dripping]

38:35.458 --> 38:36.875
[through TV] We'll find each other.

38:37.667 --> 38:39.375
Just follow the slime.

38:40.417 --> 38:41.875
[chattering through TV]

38:45.708 --> 38:47.083
[Morrow] Did you figure it out?

38:52.208 --> 38:53.375
My riddle.

38:54.333 --> 38:55.625
I figured out yours.

38:56.750 --> 38:58.083
Who is that?

39:00.000 --> 39:01.333
[techno music playing]

39:01.417 --> 39:04.625
When is a machine not a machine?

39:10.583 --> 39:12.083
I don't want to talk to you.

39:13.542 --> 39:16.458
I know. I'm sorry if I scared you before.

39:17.500 --> 39:19.083
I hadn't figured it out yet.

39:19.875 --> 39:20.917
You.

39:21.583 --> 39:22.958
Is there any way I can make it up?

39:23.042 --> 39:25.125
[breathing shakily]
Just leave me alone, please.

39:26.625 --> 39:27.833
Please.

39:32.208 --> 39:33.708
[chattering through TV]

39:35.083 --> 39:36.750
[breathing shakily]

39:42.542 --> 39:44.083
[Morrow] Ask me how I figured it out.

39:48.042 --> 39:49.125
[sniffs]

39:50.417 --> 39:51.583
Figured what out?

39:51.667 --> 39:52.792
Your riddle.

39:53.458 --> 39:55.708
How can a synthetic being have parents?

39:55.792 --> 39:57.750
I'm-I'm not supposed to talk about that.

39:57.833 --> 40:00.167
Said the child to the stranger.

40:01.000 --> 40:02.333
I'm not a child.

40:06.000 --> 40:07.333
Well, let me ask you this.

40:08.250 --> 40:09.708
How old are you?

40:14.000 --> 40:15.000
Mmm?

40:17.458 --> 40:19.042
I'm a parent, you know.

40:20.458 --> 40:21.542
A father.

40:22.375 --> 40:24.500
I was. I had a little girl.

40:25.375 --> 40:26.875
She hated raisins.

40:31.292 --> 40:32.417
I have to go.

40:32.500 --> 40:33.708
Of course. Yeah.

40:33.792 --> 40:35.208
-We'll talk tomorrow.
-No!

40:36.125 --> 40:40.042
No. [stammers] I mean, no, I can't.

40:42.667 --> 40:47.000
You know, you said something
very wise to me before.

40:47.917 --> 40:48.958
Do you remember?

40:54.667 --> 40:56.750
"Everybody needs a friend."

40:58.583 --> 41:00.250
Will you be my friend?

41:08.917 --> 41:09.917
Please?

41:15.958 --> 41:17.333
Okay.

41:20.417 --> 41:23.667
Thank you. I feel so much better now.

41:25.875 --> 41:28.500
Sleep tight. Don't let the bed bugs bite.

41:49.083 --> 41:50.083
Hello?

42:25.417 --> 42:27.125
[child Nibs] When do we get to go home?

42:29.708 --> 42:30.750
[Mother] We don't.

42:37.708 --> 42:39.875
[liquid spraying]

43:02.375 --> 43:06.125
[ominous music playing]

43:13.750 --> 43:14.833
[music stops]

43:28.250 --> 43:30.250
[high pitched ringing]

43:46.417 --> 43:47.667
[device chimes]

43:47.750 --> 43:49.333
[ringing stops]

43:57.917 --> 44:00.250
[aliens chirping]

44:26.417 --> 44:29.417
-[heart monitor beeping]
-[oxygen pumping]

44:53.708 --> 44:55.125
[aliens chirping]

45:07.292 --> 45:09.375
[keypad beeping]

45:22.208 --> 45:23.458
[door closes]

45:26.750 --> 45:28.250
[cart humming]

45:55.500 --> 45:58.542
[Kirsh] I've selected an egg
approximately 54 centimeters wide.

45:58.625 --> 46:01.000
It's 77 centimeters tall.

46:03.792 --> 46:05.708
Come in close
on the incision point, please.

46:06.542 --> 46:08.500
T, get the suction tube.

46:11.625 --> 46:14.542
[inhales deeply]
If it tries to escape, vacuum it up.

46:26.500 --> 46:29.000
[aliens chirping]

46:39.292 --> 46:42.292
[saw whirring]

46:53.875 --> 46:56.208
[buzzing]

47:09.792 --> 47:11.250
[alien chirping]

47:11.333 --> 47:13.333
[buzzing continues]

47:22.500 --> 47:25.292
[screeching]

47:35.375 --> 47:36.583
[screeching]

47:36.667 --> 47:38.167
[grunting]

47:39.833 --> 47:40.833
[groans]

47:43.500 --> 47:44.625
[screeching]

47:47.708 --> 47:50.083
[oxygen pumping]

47:50.167 --> 47:51.417
[screeching]

47:55.417 --> 47:57.000
[chirping, buzzing intensifies]

48:00.792 --> 48:01.792
[electricity crackles]

48:01.875 --> 48:03.292
-[alien screeches]
-[groans]

48:03.375 --> 48:04.375
[screeching stops]

48:05.250 --> 48:06.250
[breathing heavily]

48:40.500 --> 48:42.500
-[buzzing]
-[screams]

48:44.458 --> 48:46.042
[grunts, breathes heavily]

48:48.500 --> 48:50.250
[crackles]

49:04.333 --> 49:05.833
[alien chirping]

49:05.917 --> 49:07.250
[breathing heavily]

49:14.708 --> 49:16.958
-[alien screeching]
-[groans]

49:33.875 --> 49:35.125
[thuds]

49:56.500 --> 49:59.500
[breathing]

50:26.000 --> 50:27.500
[suspenseful music plays]

50:30.000 --> 50:32.500
["Wherever I May Roam" playing]

51:39.208 --> 51:42.750
♪ And the road becomes my bride ♪

51:42.833 --> 51:46.458
♪ And the road becomes my bride ♪

51:46.542 --> 51:49.958
♪ I have stripped of all but pride ♪

51:50.042 --> 51:53.792
♪ So in her I do confide ♪

51:53.875 --> 51:57.208
♪ And she keeps me satisfied ♪

51:57.958 --> 52:00.042
♪ Gives me all I need ♪

52:01.167 --> 52:04.292
♪ And with dust in throat I crave ♪

52:04.792 --> 52:08.375
♪ Only knowledge will I save ♪

52:08.458 --> 52:11.792
♪ To the game you stay a slave ♪

52:12.542 --> 52:16.208
♪ Rover, wanderer, nomad, vagabond ♪

52:16.292 --> 52:19.708
♪ Call me what you will, yeah ♪

52:21.375 --> 52:25.542
♪ Wherever I may roam ♪

52:28.708 --> 52:33.375
♪ Wherever I may roam, yeah ♪

52:36.000 --> 52:43.000
♪ Wherever I may wander, wander, wander ♪

52:43.083 --> 52:47.167
♪ Wherever I may roam ♪

52:47.250 --> 52:49.417
[song ends]
